 "summary": "Enacts various provisions relating to procurement procedures.",
 "title": "Enacts various provisions relating to procurement procedures",
 "vetoMessages": {
  "items": [
   {
    "billId": {
     "basePrintNo": "A8156",
     "basePrintNoStr": "A8156-2017",
     "printNo": "A8156",
     "session": 2017,
     "version": ""
    },
    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 336\n \nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nAssembly Bill Number 8156, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the state finance law and the legislative law, in\n      relation to participation by state agencies in a  system  used  by\n      the  comptroller  to compile vendor responsibility information; in\n      relation  to  defining  information  technology  for   procurement\n      purposes;  in  relation  to  authorizing  the  commissioner of the\n      office of general services and state agencies to develop  alterna-\n      tive  procurement  methods  not  otherwise authorized by law under\n      certain circumstances;  in  relation  to  authorizing  competitive\n      negotiation concluding with a best and final offer; in relation to\n      clarifying  the  use  of best and final offers for invitations for\n      bids and requests for proposals for goods, services and  technolo-\n      gy;  in relation to clarifying the use of contracts let by another\n      governmental agency; in relation to clarifying  the  valuation  of\n      non-cash  contracts  by  the state comptroller; and in relation to\n      conforming the definition of restricted period\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would amend and add  various  statutory  provisions  to  the\nState  Finance  Law  relating  to the public procurement of commodities,\nservices, technology, and public works.\n \n  While the bill purports \"to improve the State's procurement process by\nincreasing transparency, efficiency and flexibility,\" in actuality,  the\nproposed  changes  would have the opposite effect. I have vetoed similar\nbills in prior years for the  same  reasons,  particularly  because  the\nproposed amendments would place unnecessary limitations and restrictions\non  State  procurements.  (See,  Veto  No.  303 of 2015, Veto No. 295 of\n2016).   Specifically, the bill,  among  other  things,  seeks  to:  (i)\nmandate  agency  use  of  the Comptroller's online vendor responsibility\nsystem thereby limiting the  ability  of  agencies  to  seek  additional\ninformation  or  obtain paper questionnaires from vendors, such as small\nbusinesses that may not elect or are unable to use  the  online  system;\n(ii)  include  provisions that would limit situations where agencies may\nask for best and final offers thus conflicting  with  current  practice,\nimpeding  competitive  negotiations,  and  complicating the \"best value\"\nselection  process;  and  (iii)  limit  the  use  of  \"piggybacking\"  on\ncontracts,  a  valuable  tool  used  by  State agencies for more than 20\nyears, which allows for the leveraging of contracts for commodities  and\nservice  made  by  other public entities in a more timely, economic, and\nefficient way.  These proposed changes have been  advanced  without  any\napparent  justification  to  warrant  such limitations. Given the opera-\ntional and policy concerns that must be addressed, and  consistent  with\npast  practice,  State agencies should be consulted on a bill that would\nplace significant, and unnecessary,  limitations  on  their  ability  to\nconduct  public procurements. The proposed changes to the State procure-\nment laws should be made in the course of annual  State  budget  negoti-\nations.\n \n  As  there have been limited changes from previously disapproved bills,\nand for the reasons stated above, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 336,
